{
  "text": " And then I see media every day championing the safe and effective. The amount of times I heard safe and effective from this prior panel that was before me is absolutely disgusting. Because I just had to listen to someone from a public health agency present a paper, a review paper saying that they could only find a sore arm and a little muscle pain with meningococcal vaccine. That is absurd. Even in the inserts, they describe, you know, high incidence of severe life altering illnesses. There are deaths reported. We know of major adverse events around this. And she's literally going to come here and testify before you that all they have to worry about is a sore arm for disease in Wisconsin. We're literally six cases in 2016, four in 2017, only one from the strain that that vaccine addresses. So you're going to tell me we're going to force vaccinate, mandate against hundreds of thousands of kids to go after that one kid who died with a strain. And in order for that to actually make any sense, you'd have to believe what that doctor or person believes. You'd have to believe that its safety is so unparalleled that there's nothing to see here. This is good sound medical judgment.",
